      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T20:21:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. For kFilterBox, ScaleSlope() sets y \u003d 0, so uy \u003d 0 \u003c\u003d max_y on entry. Inside the loop, uy is clamped to max_y immediately after uy +\u003d dy and before the subtraction, and nothing else modifies it, so uy \u003c\u003d max_y holds at the top of every iteration. Hence (uy \u003e\u003e 16) \u003e\u003d iy and the subtraction is never negative.",
      "parentUuid": "da92dce3_14aa0526",
